schema: test/v2
level: working-unit
epic: E-CRSCOPE
wu: E-CRSCOPE.W1
branch: wu/crscope/worktree-cache-slot
tests:
  unit:
    count: 8
    where: "xtask/src/gate0.rs (5 over the cache) + xtask/src/git.rs (3 over slot resolution)"
    note: "Cache: each slot keeps its own key while a third, never-gated slot reads None; an absent cache reads None; a stored key round-trips and lives under target/; a different key is a miss; and the pre-slot cache file survives a store, because worktrees share target/debug/xtask and a checkout still running the older binary keeps writing it. Slot resolution: a linked worktree named `main` resolves to worktrees/main and never to the main checkout's slot; a repository whose own directory is called `worktrees` still owns the `main` slot (the round-1 regression, written failing first - left \"worktrees/.git\", right \"main\"); --separate-git-dir resolves by equality rather than by path shape; a git dir outside the common dir is refused rather than guessed into a slot; and the checkout that owns the repository takes `main` against real git."
  integration:
    count: 3
    where: "xtask/tests/gate0_cache.rs - three new tests, 8 in the file"
    note: "The two-worktree contract, each test building two real git worktrees whose target/ symlinks meet in one directory - what .gitworktreecopy provisions for real with `~> target`, built by hand because these fixture repos install no hooks. Alternating gates keep both skips (the trees deliberately diverge, so the two keys differ and the alternation is an eviction test rather than a repeat of one key); a tree change re-runs only the worktree that changed; and a worktree that never gated cannot consume another's green even when the two keys are byte-identical, which is the hardest case and the one a shared slot passes wrongly. A fourth, pre-existing test was rewritten here: a_gitignored_file_does_not_change_the_key now writes target/.gate0/worktrees/... rather than the pre-slot path this WU made stale - a test whose subject is 'the cache's own file' must name the file the cache uses."
  e2e:
    waived: "Gate tooling with no user-facing flow - no proxy, API or UI behaviour is delivered or changed, so there is no end-to-end path to drive. The epic's own e2e, per its plan, is a full review run under the adopted configuration asserting verdict parity; W1 delivers no configuration and cannot carry it."
verified:
  - "cargo xtask gate0 - green at the tip (fmt --check + clippy --workspace -D warnings + tests), re-run from a FORCED REBUILD after the stale-binary hazard below was caught corrupting an earlier run."
  - "242 lib tests + 8 in gate0_cache, all green, counted after `find xtask/src xtask/tests -name '*.rs' -exec touch {} +`."
  - "cargo-nextest is absent on this machine, so the gate takes its documented cargo test fallback. Recorded because the epic plan requires every number to name its runner."
  - "Mutation-checked, not assumed: forcing one shared slot fails all three integration tests and each_slot_keeps_its_own_key; pointing the slot root back at .gate0-green fails the pre-slot coexistence test; removing the .gitignore fails the rewritten gitignore test. Every new or changed test was watched to fail against the behaviour it pins."
  - "The round-1 correctness regression test was written FIRST and observed failing (left \"worktrees/.git\", right \"main\") before the fix, per the testing standard's rule for a correctness defect."
  - "Live demonstration on the real fleet, six worktrees on one target/: gate A 66.5s, gate B 45.3s, gate A again 0.49s (skip), gate B again 0.47s (skip). The third run was a full re-run before this WU. The second worktree was provisioned at this tip and removed afterwards."
  - "cargo xtask verify-doc green on docs/work/2026-09-06-crscope-w1-result.html (wu-result) and the amended DEC-11 file."
  - "cargo check --target aarch64-pc-windows-msvc -p xtask --tests: the four dead-code warnings this test target emitted before round 3's gating are gone; the two that remain are mr.rs's own and pre-existing. The Windows std is not installed here, so this is a lint-level check and not a full build - stated rather than implied."
note: "Four review rounds; every round until the last found something in the round before it. Twelve candidates, five verified (one correctness, four hygiene), seven refuted on evidence. THE MEASUREMENT HAZARD THIS WU HIT ITSELF: worktrees share target/debug/xtask and one target/, so cargo can judge a sibling's artifacts fresh and run them as yours. It happened twice here - first two neighbours' gates wrote slots using this branch's xtask minutes after it was built, then cargo test in this worktree ran a stale binary omitting four tests that exist in the source, reporting 238 lib tests where the tree holds 242. Round 3's altitude sweep independently traced that 238 to sibling worktree TRA-RFINISH-W3, which holds exactly 238 tests and whose target/ resolves to the same physical directory. The consequence is that Gate 0 can report green for code it never compiled - its cached key is sound about the TREE and cannot see whose binaries ran. Every number in this note was therefore re-taken from a forced rebuild rather than left standing. It is recorded as a follow-up and deliberately not fixed here: it is gate soundness rather than the cache, and widening the WU into it is the scope creep the epic's non-goals forbid."
